# Backend Rules

- Keep routes/controllers thin. Put business rules in application/domain services.
- Put database access behind repositories. Do not write SQL in route handlers.
- Validate params, query strings, bodies, and upload metadata at the API boundary.
- Use shared Zod contracts wherever practical.
- Enforce status transitions in backend services.
- Keep original intake answers and original extracted text immutable after submission.
- Use generated UUID storage keys; never derive filesystem paths from user input.
- Store uploaded files outside public static directories.
- Verify file signatures/content, MIME, extension, file size, and PDF page limits.
- Reject unsupported formats and oversized files with typed errors.
- Never expose filesystem paths in API responses.
- Do not log request bodies, patient data, extracted text, AI prompts/output, or secrets.
- Return consistent error envelopes and appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Configure request body limits, upload limits, and processing timeouts.
- Demo API is unauthenticated: bind to localhost for local use and use synthetic data only.
